## Design direction

A challenge coin format that integrates a bottle-opening feature into the outline while retaining space for two-sided identity and commemorative artwork.

For custom bottle opener challenge coins, begin with the part of the artwork that must read first. Keep the outline, smallest lettering, color breaks and functional details clear, then use finish and presentation to support the design rather than compete with it.

## Confirmed choices and project decisions

- Base materials for double-sided coins include zinc alloy and iron.
- Edge choices include flat, 2D or 3D rope, diamond cross cut, oblique or swirl cut, spur or petal, bezel, reeded, and laser text.
- Standard packaging is an OPP bag; optional packaging includes a printed card, plastic capsule, velvet box, PVC bag, velvet pouch, and wooden box.

## Preparing your brief

Send the artwork, intended dimensions, quantity, delivery destination and required timing. Note which surfaces, moving parts, attachments or packaging details matter most so the quotation can be based on one clear specification.

Golden One will use the approved brief as the basis for the final product specification; unconfirmed materials, claims and performance details are not assumed.
